WEBVTT

00:03.740 --> 00:05.180
What's wrong?

00:05.180 --> 00:06.440
Hey.

00:06.440 --> 00:08.190
Haru-kun?

00:10.650 --> 00:11.960
Hey!

00:12.550 --> 00:14.280
Come on, please say something!

00:14.490 --> 00:15.780
Haru-kun!

00:38.140 --> 00:44.850
Shining stars away bless

00:45.190 --> 00:50.070
chiisakutonaeru mahou no kotobawa

00:45.190 --> 00:50.070
Silently chanting the magical words

00:50.940 --> 00:52.690
『onegai。。。』

00:50.940 --> 00:52.690
"please"

00:52.990 --> 00:58.320
hoshizora samayou kaze ni notta maigo notsubu

00:52.990 --> 00:58.320
The lost grain riding the wind on the sky

00:58.320 --> 00:59.370
『kizuite。。。』

00:58.320 --> 00:59.370
Please notice

00:59.370 --> 01:07.250
tsutawara nakute porori ochita kono omoi

00:59.370 --> 01:07.250
Untold words, teardrops of feelings that fell down

01:07.750 --> 01:14.340
kagayaki dasuyo GARASU bin nonaka

01:07.750 --> 01:14.340
Show your shine inside the glass bottle

01:14.720 --> 01:21.720
manten no hoshi deatta KISEKI kimi ga soba ni itekureru nara

01:14.720 --> 01:21.720
If you will stay beside me perfect star of encountered miracles...

01:21.890 --> 01:29.110
Whatever the mystery, I will be able to gather my courage.

01:22.310 --> 01:29.110
donna fushigi mouke tomeru yuuki umare te yuku yo

01:29.440 --> 01:36.700
nanatsuiro ni hikaru houseki sora kara mai oriru

01:29.440 --> 01:36.700
Seven colored glittering gems flying down from the sky

01:36.700 --> 01:40.410
Scoop up the important fragments

01:37.110 --> 01:40.410
daijina KAKERA sukui agerune

01:40.410 --> 01:45.910
kowasa nuyou sotto。。。

01:40.410 --> 01:45.910
And secretly hold onto them tight

02:11.270 --> 02:14.210
I'm sorry, Haru-kun.

02:16.740 --> 02:19.130
I'm sorry.

02:27.350 --> 02:32.480
I know I shouldn't cry, but...

02:33.760 --> 02:36.140
It's hard to endure...

02:36.140 --> 02:39.030
Because it's Haru-kun.

02:40.750 --> 02:42.420
Sumomo-chan...

02:44.410 --> 02:49.470
I'm sorry. I shouldn't keep on crying.

02:51.310 --> 02:53.870
You know, Sumomo-chan...

02:53.870 --> 02:57.740
Everyone has something that they like or treasure.

02:57.740 --> 02:59.080
Yes.

02:59.080 --> 03:03.630
And for everyone, there is something they must do everyday.

03:03.630 --> 03:05.610
For me, it's work...

03:05.610 --> 03:08.370
And for Sumomo-chan and Nako-chan, it's school.

03:08.370 --> 03:09.380
Yes.

03:10.270 --> 03:11.340
But you know...

03:11.340 --> 03:14.650
Sometimes, there are times where you throw away everything,

03:14.650 --> 03:17.760
and protect the thing that is important to you.

03:17.760 --> 03:19.220
Sometimes...

03:21.720 --> 03:24.950
When that happens even if you cry or scream...

03:24.950 --> 03:27.560
it is nothing to be ashamed of.

03:27.560 --> 03:28.850
That's right.

03:32.280 --> 03:35.110
S-Sensei...

03:37.060 --> 03:39.440
Nako-chan.

03:39.440 --> 03:42.940
You don't need to push yourself, Sumomo.

03:43.980 --> 03:45.590
Nako-chan!

03:49.090 --> 03:52.300
Haru-kun... Haru-kun did it for me...

03:53.380 --> 03:55.290
I... I...

04:01.510 --> 04:05.430
Silver Colored Full Moon

04:09.570 --> 04:14.730
And for that reason, Tsuwabuki-kun was hospitalized at the local hospital.

04:14.730 --> 04:16.620
Tsuwabuki hospitalized?

04:16.620 --> 04:18.230
Leave of absence, they say.

04:17.820 --> 04:20.030
Isn't he going out with Akihime?

04:20.030 --> 04:20.990
Seriously?

04:20.990 --> 04:26.790
Well, even though I say hospitalization, he is just getting rest so there is no need to worry.

04:29.280 --> 04:30.330
Well then...

04:32.660 --> 04:33.880
Sumomo-chan.

04:33.880 --> 04:35.680
Sumomo-chan went to visit, right?

04:35.680 --> 04:37.320
Tsuwabuki, how was he?

04:38.190 --> 04:40.680
He was fine a few days ago, wasn't he?

04:40.680 --> 04:42.080
Just what kind of illness...

04:42.080 --> 04:45.640
Truthfully, it wasn't something that even needed visiting.

04:45.640 --> 04:47.190
Right, Sumomo?

04:47.190 --> 04:48.030
Yeah.

04:48.030 --> 04:50.020
But, but...

04:50.020 --> 04:52.210
Sumomo-chan, you must be worrying a lot.

04:52.210 --> 04:53.390
Right?

04:53.390 --> 04:55.490
Why did he suddenly...?

04:55.490 --> 04:57.940
I'm alright.

04:57.940 --> 05:00.270
Haru-kun will come back soon.

05:03.250 --> 05:06.330
I'm sure that... pretty soon...

05:06.330 --> 05:07.780
I'm sure...

05:18.800 --> 05:21.670
<i>Even though it's my fault,</i>

05:21.670 --> 05:22.930
<i>why...</i>

05:23.850 --> 05:24.630
Yuuki.

05:30.270 --> 05:30.970
What?

05:34.040 --> 05:36.370
Sumomo doesn't...

05:37.300 --> 05:41.530
No, she doesn't blame Yuuki at the slightest.

05:43.330 --> 05:44.540
Therefore...

05:45.130 --> 05:48.450
Therefore, you don't need to be so hard on yourself.

06:28.670 --> 06:30.540
This Recipe is...

06:31.330 --> 06:33.050
Could it be...?

06:33.050 --> 06:36.000
Impossible. It's too difficult.

06:36.000 --> 06:38.350
Sumomo-chan can't...

06:43.280 --> 06:44.490
But...

06:56.730 --> 06:58.860
You've cleaned much better today than before.

06:58.860 --> 07:00.190
Thank you, Matsuda.

07:00.190 --> 07:04.160
No, what I did was something a butler should do.

07:05.520 --> 07:07.900
Thank you for doing this for me, Matsuda.

07:07.900 --> 07:10.030
It is an honor!

07:11.340 --> 07:13.800
Miss, Matsuda is working very hard-

07:15.410 --> 07:16.230
Miss!

07:17.130 --> 07:18.850
What seems to be the problem?

07:18.850 --> 07:20.930
To return this early...

07:20.930 --> 07:24.170
If you'd have called, I would've gone straight away to pick you up.

07:24.170 --> 07:28.030
But more importantly, are you feeling sick or something?

07:28.030 --> 07:29.690
Should I bring some medicine?

07:29.690 --> 07:32.100
Or maybe something war-

07:34.040 --> 07:35.970
M-Miss.

07:35.970 --> 07:37.970
What happened, Miss?

07:37.980 --> 07:39.150
Miss!

07:40.390 --> 07:43.080
Haru-kun will come back soon.

07:43.640 --> 07:46.460
I'm sure that... pretty soon...

07:46.460 --> 07:48.070
I'm sure...

07:49.180 --> 07:50.860
It's my fault, isn't it?

07:50.860 --> 07:53.110
It's natural that I should take the blame.

07:55.180 --> 08:00.580
Why? Why aren't you even blaming me at all?

08:03.660 --> 08:05.830
So, Sumomo-chan...

08:05.830 --> 08:10.580
You said you were able to use the Recipe called "Timu Forna Mei," right?

08:10.580 --> 08:11.750
Yes.

08:11.750 --> 08:16.400
It was like things around me slowed down.

08:17.080 --> 08:20.520
Well, there is a more advanced Recipe.

08:20.520 --> 08:24.370
If you can use a Recipe called "Tim Forna Principatu,"

08:24.370 --> 08:28.710
you might be able to turn back Yuki's time.

08:28.710 --> 08:32.780
And if you return to the time before he revealed his identity,

08:33.410 --> 08:35.840
Tsuwabuki-kun might be able to return.

08:35.840 --> 08:37.200
Is that true?

08:37.490 --> 08:38.840
But this...

08:40.180 --> 08:44.220
This is a very difficult Recipe.

08:44.220 --> 08:46.900
I'm not sure how well it will go.

08:46.900 --> 08:48.090
Sumomo.

08:48.300 --> 08:52.290
Sensei, I'll... I'll do it.

08:52.290 --> 08:55.340
No matter how difficult it may be...

08:55.590 --> 08:58.020
If I don't do it, Haru-kun will...

08:59.900 --> 09:01.410
Haru-kun will...

09:11.450 --> 09:15.860
Well then, for Figurare's power to be at its fullest...

09:17.900 --> 09:19.110
Yes.

09:21.530 --> 09:24.030
Let's do it when the moon is full.

09:31.030 --> 09:33.780
<i>Sumomo doesn't...</i>

09:34.210 --> 09:38.220
<i>No, she doesn't blame Yuuki at the slightest.</i>

09:40.960 --> 09:44.660
Miss, I brought some hot tea.

09:44.660 --> 09:45.870
Miss?

09:47.980 --> 09:50.140
Where are you going?

10:46.280 --> 10:48.120
That light is...

11:00.650 --> 11:04.130
Timu Forna Principatu

11:18.540 --> 11:20.370
Are you okay?

11:20.370 --> 11:23.000
You've been practicing this so much. You're tired, aren't you?

11:23.000 --> 11:27.910
It's very difficult to control.

11:27.910 --> 11:29.910
But I want to keep trying a little harder.

11:30.420 --> 11:32.010
Sumomo...

11:35.690 --> 11:38.510
Timu Forna Principatu.

11:40.170 --> 11:41.780
Impossible.

11:41.780 --> 11:44.440
There's no way that it'll work.

11:45.330 --> 11:46.620
But...

12:22.860 --> 12:25.620
<i>No matter how much I try, it isn't going well. </i>

12:25.620 --> 12:26.910
<i>And...</i>

12:26.910 --> 12:31.200
<i>It's harder than any of the Recipes I've used so far.</i>

12:32.310 --> 12:33.770
<i>Sumomo...</i>

12:35.720 --> 12:37.860
<i>To be that tired... </i>

12:37.860 --> 12:41.690
<i>It's not surprising... for such a difficult Recipe.</i>

12:42.580 --> 12:43.740
Miss.

12:43.740 --> 12:45.620
What seems to be the problem?

12:45.620 --> 12:47.360
To suddenly say that you wish to go to the kitchen...

12:47.770 --> 12:51.240
And lately, you've been going out alone at night.

12:51.240 --> 12:53.950
It's not to collect stardrops either, and...

12:53.950 --> 12:56.870
Ah! If there is a need for a boxed lunch, I will gladly prepare it.

12:56.870 --> 12:58.640
Then there's no point!

12:58.640 --> 12:59.380
Yes?

13:01.610 --> 13:02.630
Matsuda!

13:02.630 --> 13:03.630
Y-Yes?

13:04.640 --> 13:07.770
C-Cooking, how do you do it?

13:11.960 --> 13:13.970
<i>One more night...</i>

13:13.970 --> 13:15.890
<i>Tonight, without a doubt...</i>

13:16.610 --> 13:21.020
<i>I'll control time to make the withered flower blossom.</i>

13:21.480 --> 13:26.070
Timu Forna Principatu

13:41.650 --> 13:43.420
I did it!

13:44.380 --> 13:45.430
You did it!

13:45.430 --> 13:46.600
Amazing, Sumomo.

13:46.600 --> 13:47.700
You made it in time.

13:47.700 --> 13:50.130
Yeah, thanks Nako-chan.

13:50.130 --> 13:51.750
You've done well.

13:54.490 --> 13:55.400
Sumomo?

13:55.910 --> 13:59.440
I'm okay. It's just that I'm out of strength.

13:59.440 --> 14:02.110
Sumomo, to do it up to this point...

14:04.190 --> 14:05.610
Thanks.

14:05.610 --> 14:09.190
It's because Nako-chan kept encouraging me.

14:09.190 --> 14:11.210
No, Sumomo gave it her best, that's why.

14:11.210 --> 14:13.750
I'm sure that everything will go just fine tomorrow.

14:13.750 --> 14:14.950
Yeah.

14:30.130 --> 14:31.630
Hot!

14:31.630 --> 14:32.440
Miss!

14:32.440 --> 14:34.620
A-A-Are you okay?

14:34.620 --> 14:36.560
Matsuda will take care of this...

14:36.560 --> 14:38.560
I'm fine, let's continue.

14:38.560 --> 14:41.120
But Miss...

14:53.410 --> 14:56.060
At last, tonight...

14:56.060 --> 14:59.800
If I... If I fail...

15:00.380 --> 15:02.510
It's possible, if it is Sumomo.

15:02.510 --> 15:03.870
Yuki-chan.

15:03.870 --> 15:05.870
You can definitely do it, Sumomo.

15:05.870 --> 15:07.040
Haru-kun.

15:12.550 --> 15:15.670
I'm scared, Haru-kun.

15:22.610 --> 15:24.330
Sumomo!

15:29.220 --> 15:30.400
Akihime.

15:30.400 --> 15:32.030
No!

15:44.650 --> 15:45.960
Yuki-chan.

16:26.590 --> 16:28.210
Mother?

16:40.160 --> 16:43.730
Oh my, I fell asleep.

16:46.870 --> 16:48.350
Huh?

16:49.190 --> 16:50.360
This is...

16:51.840 --> 16:54.760
Eat this and do well.

16:54.760 --> 16:59.770
There's no point if you collapse before you save Tsuwabuki, is there?

17:00.900 --> 17:03.030
Yuuki Nona.

17:04.400 --> 17:05.870
Nona-chan.

17:11.200 --> 17:16.840
I couldn't eat these past few days.

17:19.110 --> 17:21.360
Thank you, Nona-chan.

17:21.360 --> 17:22.870
It's delicious.

17:28.360 --> 17:33.790
This is a magic circle which amplifies the power of your spell.

17:33.790 --> 17:35.400
Now, Sumomo-chan,

17:35.400 --> 17:37.100
put Yuki-chan down in the middle.

17:37.100 --> 17:38.300
Yes.

17:42.140 --> 17:43.530
Yuki-chan.

17:44.110 --> 17:45.410
Haru-kun.

17:45.690 --> 17:47.210
Please wait for me.

17:54.600 --> 17:59.110
It'd be great if the ability of the Ladle could be amplified from this.

17:59.110 --> 18:01.650
Now, swinging the Ladle in front of Yuki-chan,

18:01.650 --> 18:03.670
and reciting the Recipe is all that's left.

18:03.670 --> 18:04.760
Good luck.

18:04.760 --> 18:05.960
Yes.

18:06.840 --> 18:10.060
Nako-chan, sorry to make you worry all the time.

18:10.060 --> 18:11.360
I'm sure it will go well.

18:12.120 --> 18:13.420
Sumomo.

18:14.380 --> 18:16.370
Yeah, good luck to you.

18:27.100 --> 18:29.630
Sensei, Nako-chan.

18:29.970 --> 18:32.170
And Nona-chan.

18:32.610 --> 18:33.830
Thank you.

18:38.090 --> 18:39.330
Sumomo.

18:39.820 --> 18:41.470
Sumomo-chan.

18:44.690 --> 18:49.660
Timu Forna Principatu!

19:11.810 --> 19:13.040
Sumomo!

19:11.810 --> 19:13.040
Sumomo-chan!

19:24.650 --> 19:26.910
Pull yourself together, Prima Plam!

19:27.360 --> 19:29.020
You can't lose!

19:29.020 --> 19:32.000
You're going to meet him, Tsuwabuki, aren't you?!

19:32.000 --> 19:36.780
Aspalas-san... No. Nona-chan.

19:36.780 --> 19:38.060
Yes!

19:51.350 --> 19:52.840
Do your best.

19:54.850 --> 19:58.590
It's okay. It'll definitely work.

19:58.590 --> 20:00.790
If it is you two...

20:00.790 --> 20:02.170
Have faith.

20:04.870 --> 20:06.280
That was...

20:07.280 --> 20:08.520
Now!

20:09.220 --> 20:10.030
Right!

20:11.440 --> 20:13.320
<i>Yuki-chan, thank you.</i>

20:13.320 --> 20:17.230
<i>Haru-kun, come back.</i>

20:30.190 --> 20:31.450
Yuuki.

20:31.780 --> 20:34.330
It's fine. It definitely was a success.

20:37.080 --> 20:39.080
Haru-kun.

20:44.530 --> 20:46.090
Sumomo.

20:47.140 --> 20:49.350
Haru-kun.

20:57.810 --> 21:00.630
Umm, Sumomo?

21:00.630 --> 21:03.850
Is this... the school's grounds?

21:03.850 --> 21:06.360
Eh. Sumomo? Sumomo?

21:06.360 --> 21:10.380
We'll tell you all about it later, Tsuwabuki.

21:10.380 --> 21:13.060
Yaeno, Yuuki too.

21:18.040 --> 21:21.600
I'm sorry to call you all the way here.

21:21.600 --> 21:23.900
It wasn't because of me.

21:23.900 --> 21:26.300
It was because of the strength of those two girls.

21:26.300 --> 21:29.120
Those two are really amazing.

21:31.740 --> 21:34.560
Sensei, thank you very much.

21:34.800 --> 21:38.240
No, it's the result of Sumomo-chan's effort.

21:38.240 --> 21:41.000
The power of love really is invincible.

21:41.000 --> 21:42.630
Sumomo!

21:42.630 --> 21:44.740
Yuuki said she'll give us rides!

21:46.840 --> 21:49.860
I'll go thank Nona-chan.

21:49.860 --> 21:51.090
Well then...

21:51.390 --> 21:52.790
Tsuwabuki-kun.

21:53.310 --> 21:54.660
Yes?

21:56.830 --> 21:59.060
I'll ask just in case, but...

21:59.060 --> 22:00.970
Right now...

22:01.430 --> 22:02.710
What month is it?

22:02.710 --> 22:05.340
Umm, what month you say?

22:10.550 --> 22:13.500
It's May.

22:17.620 --> 22:21.910
Right now, it's November... Tsuwabuki-kun.

22:51.590 --> 22:55.140
kira kira no hoshikuzu ha maru de

22:51.590 --> 22:55.140
Fragments of glittering stars

22:55.140 --> 22:58.430
koi suru otome no kiseki

22:55.140 --> 22:58.430
are just like the miracles of a girl in love

22:58.690 --> 23:02.230
kinou mada no watashi ha doko he

22:58.690 --> 23:02.230
Where did the cleverness from yesterday go,

23:02.230 --> 23:05.150
nanika chigau RABIRINSU

23:02.230 --> 23:05.150
Since it's like a labyrinth now

23:05.650 --> 23:09.400
dan dan wakan naku naru

23:05.650 --> 23:09.400
Slowly becoming confused

23:09.570 --> 23:12.410
（doushi you　doushi you）

23:09.570 --> 23:12.410
What do I do? What do I do?

23:12.660 --> 23:19.620
don don afurete kuru　AH　HAHAHA

23:12.660 --> 23:19.620
Slowly becoming overflowed

23:19.790 --> 23:25.500
yume no naka jya　nandemo ieru no ni…

23:19.790 --> 23:25.500
But inside a dream, can't you say anything?

23:25.500 --> 23:29.130
yuuki kudasai

23:25.500 --> 23:29.130
Please give me courage

23:30.430 --> 23:32.050
mo-o！

23:30.430 --> 23:32.050
Mo-o!

23:32.220 --> 23:36.890
konna ni aitai no ni

23:32.220 --> 23:36.890
I really want to meet you

23:36.890 --> 23:39.180
kanari Bi-myo

23:36.890 --> 23:39.180
Proxy doll

23:39.350 --> 23:43.100
toki meki ga koi no saidai no teki

23:39.350 --> 23:43.100
This throbbing is love's biggest challenge

23:43.100 --> 23:44.690
jirettai no yo

23:43.100 --> 23:44.690
It's irritating

23:44.690 --> 23:46.020
ne-e

23:44.690 --> 23:46.020
Isn't it?

23:46.440 --> 23:51.150
yume kara sametara mata

23:46.440 --> 23:51.150
The reasons to wake again

23:51.150 --> 23:56.700
kobore souna kimi no egao ni

23:51.150 --> 23:56.700
Are overflowing to see your smile

23:56.700 --> 23:59.620
airu kana

23:56.700 --> 23:59.620
If we meet again

24:10.120 --> 24:12.470
What if a precious memory disappeared?

24:10.800 --> 24:12.470
Next Episode

24:12.470 --> 24:13.560
What do you mean?

24:13.560 --> 24:17.360
What if two lovers lost their memory of their time together?

24:17.820 --> 24:18.730
That is...

24:18.730 --> 24:21.510
If I lost my precious memory of being with Nobuko-san...!

24:21.480 --> 24:24.980
Episode 11

24:21.480 --> 24:24.980
Teardrop Colored Resolution

24:22.030 --> 24:22.930
Obviously...

24:22.930 --> 24:24.980
That's not it! Idiot!
